                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": 492,
                              "content": "The first part is the squared length of Xv, so it is never negative. The second is lambda times the squared length of v, which is positive whenever v is not zero. So no nonzero v is sent to zero, and the matrix is invertible.",
